WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
Seven concepts hang over
an open book: identity,

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:11.360
culture, creativity, communication,
perspective, transformation, representation.

3
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.960
Slide one across the page,
and a few words light up.

4
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.770
Slide another, and different words glow.

5
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.120
So what do you actually do
with one of these in an essay?

6
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.360
In this mission, you'll ask
what each concept is for,

7
00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.320
beyond a word to drop in.

8
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.350
You'll test some ways of using one.

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.300
A keyword?

10
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:30.560
A paragraph heading?

11
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:31.790
Something else?

12
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.730
And you'll test the lenses on Jane Eyre,
as Rochester tells her not to struggle

13
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.360
"like a wild frantic bird".

14
00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:43.630
Your mission: work out how to
use one concept in an essay.
